tervention for patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through natural food sources, facilitating their rehabilitation and enhancing their overall well-being.\",32\r\n13269,GRUPO NADYA-SENPE,\"The GRUPO NADYA-SENPE is a Spanish organization dedicated to home enteral nutrition. It functions as a working group that focuses on artificial nutrition in the home setting, engaging in various reports and studies related to enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, GRUPO NADYA-SENPE aims to enhance the understanding and implementation of enteral nutrition practices in Spain.\",5\r\n4945,NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA,\"\"\"NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA\"\" (NAD) refers to a medical intervention that provides nutritional support to patients in their own homes. This approach encompasses the administration of nutrition through enteral (NED) or parenteral (NPD) methods, aimed at improving or maintaining the nutritional status of patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. NAD is recognized as a significant advancement in the care of chronic patients, allowing them to receive necessary nutritional support without the need for hospitalization. \n\nBy enabling patients to remain in their familiar social and family environments, NAD not only enhances their nutritional status but also helps reduce potential complications associated with inadequate nutrition. The provision of nutritional support at home is documented by the Grupo NADYA-SENPE and is essential for those who cannot meet their dietary needs through natural foods. Overall, \"\"NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA\"\" plays a crucial role in the management of patients requiring specialized nutritional therapy in a home setting.\",40\r\n13236,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA,\"\"\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA\"\" refers to a form of home nutritional therapy designed for patients who can digest food but are unable to obtain sufficient nutrients through oral intake. This specific type o